em with the champion for Brasileirao 2019. The result shows \"Atletico\" with 112 points and 31W/19D/26L = 76 matches, which is wrong. This is because there are TWO Brasileirao competitions: \"Brasileirao\" (2012-2022) and \"Brasileirao (Historical)\" (2003-2019). The 2019 season exists in BOTH competitions.\n\nThe standings() function filters by `m.competition.lower() == comp_lower`. If user passes \"Brasileirao\", it matches only \"Brasileirao\" exactly (not \"Brasileirao (Historical)\"). Let me check: 2019 appears in both. For \"Brasileirao\" 2019, there should be the regular season. But the result shows 112 points and 76 matches worth of record which suggests aggregation issue.\n\nWait, 31W+19D+26L = 76. That's way more than 38 matches per team. This indicates the standings is double-counting. Actually, \"Atletico\" — there might be multiple \"Atletico\" teams (Atletico-MG, Athletico-PR) that normalize to the same key \"atletico\"! That's the bug. \"Atlético-MG\" and \"Athletico-PR\" both → \"atletico\" after stripping accents and removing non-alphanumeric. \n\nAthletico vs Atlético - these normalize differently actually:\n- \"Atlético\" → strip accents → \"Atletico\" → \"atletico\"\n- \"Athletico\" → \"athletico\"\n\nWait those are different. Let me check. Actually \"Athletico-PR\" → \"athletico\" (no, \"Athletico\" → \"athletico\"). And \"Atlético-MG\" → \"atletico\". So they ARE different. Good.\n\nBut the result shows \"Atletico\" with 76 matches. Let me check what's happening. The issue is that \"Brasileirao\" competition in 2019 — there might be many teams. Actually wait, 112 points is too high. Let me check the standings directly.\n\nActually the issue: champion returns \"Atletico\" but the real 2019 Brasileirao champion was Flamengo. Let me check more carefully. The problem may be team name collisions where multiple distinct teams normalize to the same key. Let me check \"Atletico\" key.\n\nActually, let me check: in Brasileirao_Matches.csv 2019, are there teams that both normalize to \"atletico\"? \"Atlético-MG\" → atletico. \"Athletico-PR\" → athletico. Hmm those differ. But wait, in the historical file, \"Athletico-PR\" might be spelled \"Atletico-PR\"? Let me check.\n\nActually the real issue is that for competition=\"Brasileirao\" season=\"2019\", only the \"Brasileirao\" competition matches (not historical) are used. Let me check the standings count. 112 points / 3 ≈ 37 wins... no. Let me just debug.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_058f53ff4001YUyNWtrcZ06ucp","sessionID":"ses_fa710145bffe992PbNwQxTi5bS","messageID":"msg_058f5037f001Go4z1Y4T5jar7y"}}
