{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788198977080,"sessionID":"ses_fa710145bffe992PbNwQxTi5bS","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"01a058f6e49bbe469ee1a9ef067574c6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-b02a3ecfac7e/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py","newString":"    def resolve(self, bare_key: str, state: str = \"\") -> str:\n        \"\"\"Return the canonical key for an observed (bare, state) pair.\"\"\"\n        if not bare_key:\n            return \"\"\n        st = (state or \"\").strip().upper()\n        states = self._bare_states.get(bare_key, set())\n        # Ambiguous bare name: state is required to disambiguate.\n        if len(states) > 1:\n            return f\"{bare_key}|{st}\" if st else bare_key\n        # Unambiguous: collapse to bare key (state is redundant).\n        return bare_key\n\n    def resolve_query_keys(self, name: str) -> list[str]:\n        \"\"\"Return all canonical keys matching a user-supplied team name.\n\n        A bare name with no state that is ambiguous (e.g. \"Atletico\") expands\n        to every state variant so the query surfaces all matching teams.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not name:\n            return []\n        bare = _bare_key(name)\n        st = extract_state(name)\n        states = self._bare_states.get(bare, set())\n        if st:\n            return [self.resolve(bare, st)]\n        if len(states) > 1:\n            return [f\"{bare}|{s}\" for s in sorted(states)]\n        return [bare]","oldString":"    def resolve(self, bare_key: str, state: str = \"\") -> str:\n        \"\"\"Return the canonical key for an observed (bare, state) pair.\"\"\"\n        if not bare_key:\n            return \"\"\n        st = (state or \"\").strip().upper()\n        states = self._bare_states.get(bare_key, set())\n        # Ambiguous bare name: state is required to disambiguate.\n        if len(states) > 1:\n            return f\"{bare_key}|{st}\" if st else bare_key\n        # Unambiguous: collapse to bare key (state is redundant).\n        return bare_key"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-b02a3ecfac7e/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-b02a3ecfac7e/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-b02a3ecfac7e/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n@@ -149,9 +149,26 @@\n             return f\"{bare_key}|{st}\" if st else bare_key\n         # Unambiguous: collapse to bare key (state is redundant).\n         return bare_key\n \n+    def resolve_query_keys(self, name: str) -> list[str]:\n+        \"\"\"Return all canonical keys matching a user-supplied team name.\n \n+        A bare name with no state that is ambiguous (e.g. \"Atletico\") expands\n+        to every state variant so the query surfaces all matching teams.\n+        \"\"\"\n+        if not name:\n+            return []\n+        bare = _bare_key(name)\n+        st = extract_state(name)\n+        states = self._bare_states.get(bare, set())\n+        if st:\n+            return [self.resolve(bare, st)]\n+        if len(states) > 1:\n+            return [f\"{bare}|{s}\" for s in sorted(states)]\n+        return [bare]\n+\n+\n # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n # Date parsing\n # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-b02a3ecfac7e/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-b02a3ecfac7e/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-b02a3ecfac7e/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-b02a3ecfac7e/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n@@ -149,9 +149,26 @@\n             return f\"{bare_key}|{st}\" if st else bare_key\n         # Unambiguous: collapse to bare key (state is redundant).\n         return bare_key\n \n+    def resolve_query_keys(self, name: str) -> list[str]:\n+        \"\"\"Return all canonical keys matching a user-supplied team name.\n \n+        A bare name with no state that is ambiguous (e.g. \"Atletico\") expands\n+        to every state variant so the query surfaces all matching teams.\n+        \"\"\"\n+        if not name:\n+            return []\n+        bare = _bare_key(name)\n+        st = extract_state(name)\n+        states = self._bare_states.get(bare, set())\n+        if st:\n+            return [self.resolve(bare, st)]\n+        if len(states) > 1:\n+            return [f\"{bare}|{s}\" for s in sorted(states)]\n+        return [bare]\n+\n+\n # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n # Date parsing\n # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n \n","additions":17,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py","time":{"start":1788198977076,"end":1788198977079}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now I need to update the queries.py to use the resolver for query-side name resolution. Currently `find_matches` etc. use `_team_key(name)` = `normalize_team_name(name)` which now returns `bare|state` if state present, else bare. But the indexed keys use the resolver which collapses unambiguous names to bare key. So if user passes \"Palmeiras-SP\", normalize_team_name returns \"palmeiras|SP\" but the indexed key is \"palmeiras\" — mismatch!\n\nI need the query side to also use the resolver. The query engine has access to `self.loader.resolver`. So `_team_key` in queries should resolve through the resolver: compute bare_key + state from the user input, then call `resolver.resolve(bare, state)`.\n\nBut there's a subtlety: if user passes \"Atletico\" (ambiguous, no state), resolver.resolve returns \"atletico\" (bare) which won't match \"atletico|MG\" or \"atletico|PR\" in the index. For ambiguous queries without state, we should match ALL teams with that bare name. \n\nLet me add a method to the resolver or query engine that returns the list of canonical keys matching a user-supplied name. Let me add `resolve_query_keys(name)` to the loader/resolver that:\n- computes bare + state\n- if state given → return [resolver.resolve(bare, state)]\n- if no state:\n  - if bare is ambiguous (multiple states) → return all canonical keys [bare|S1, bare|S2, ...]\n  - else → return [bare]\n\nLet me add this to TeamResolver.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_058f6fe2400132itOnUrEmo6Xt","sessionID":"ses_fa710145bffe992PbNwQxTi5bS","messageID":"msg_058f6c5040010axMBHa7j67ek1"}}
